-- int-tests-commencement-and-fees.l4: whole scenarios S12 and S13 of expectations.md.  The commencement chain runs from the Fees
-- Regulations (group 8) through the Law's commencement (group 7) to the Second Schedule's three-year note (group 2); the fee table
-- runs the nine services of group 8 through the six heads of s.59 (group 7), in every vintage.  Every expected value was written in
-- expectations.md from the Hebrew text before this module was run.

§ `Tests: the commencement chain and the fees`

§§ `S12. The commencement chain (groups 8, 7, 2)`

-- Regulation 5: seven days from the publication of 9.7.2025 is 16.7.2025 (IL s.10(a)); the amending regulations state no commencement, so Ordinance s.17: the day of publication, 4.5.2026.
#ASSERT `int — the Fees Regulations came into force on` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
#ASSERT `int — the amending regulations came into force on` EQUALS YMD 2026 5 4
-- s.63(a)(1): the later of three months after the publication of 14.1.2025 (14.4.2025) and 16.7.2025.
#ASSERT `int — the commencement day` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
#ASSERT `int — the day the Law commences for work on a system with any other refrigerant` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 16
#ASSERT REFUSED `int — the day Chapter 6 commences`
#ASSERT `int — the day Chapter 6 commences, section 46 regulations being in force from` (YMD 2026 6 1) EQUALS YMD 2027 1 16
#ASSERT `int — the day Chapter 6 commences, section 46 regulations being in force from` (YMD 2027 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 1
-- Chapter 6 in force: not on 15.1.2027; from 16.1.2027 the sources alone do not answer.
#ASSERT NOT `int — Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` (YMD 2027 1 15)
#ASSERT REFUSED `int — Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` (YMD 2027 1 16)
#ASSERT `int — Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act, given the facts` (YMD 2027 1 16) `fixture: the commencement facts with a hypothetical regulation under section 46`
#ASSERT NOT `int — Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act, given the facts` (YMD 2027 1 15) `fixture: the commencement facts with a hypothetical regulation under section 46`
-- The work: lawful propane (paragraph (1)) from 16.7.2025; R134a (paragraph (2)) from 16.1.2027.
#ASSERT NOT `int — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "290") (YMD 2025 7 15)
#ASSERT `int — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "290") (YMD 2025 7 16)
#ASSERT NOT `int — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a") (YMD 2027 1 15)
#ASSERT `int — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a") (YMD 2027 1 16)
-- Three years from the commencement day (the Second Schedule's note, counted from s.63(a)(1)): 16.7.2028, a Sunday.
#ASSERT `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 3 `years after an event on` `int — the commencement day` EQUALS YMD 2028 7 16
-- An applicant with 365 days of work in 2027 seeking a grade 1 licence: the experience item (item 2, up to 220 hours) is open on 16.7.2028 and closed on 17.7.2028.
`the applicant with the year 2027 of work` MEANS `fixture: an applicant with only the periods of work, being` `fixture: Dana, an individual` `and the periods` (LIST (`Period of work on cooling systems` WITH `first day of the period` IS YMD 2027 1 1, `last day of the period` IS YMD 2027 12 31))
`the items open on 16 July 2028` MEANS `int — the training the Second Schedule requires for` (`fixture: an application by` `the applicant with the year 2027 of work` `for a` `grade 1 licence` `on` (YMD 2028 7 16))
`the items open on 17 July 2028` MEANS `int — the training the Second Schedule requires for` (`fixture: an application by` `the applicant with the year 2027 of work` `for a` `grade 1 licence` `on` (YMD 2028 7 17))
#ASSERT any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number` EQUALS 2) `the items open on 16 July 2028`
#ASSERT NOT any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number` EQUALS 2) `the items open on 17 July 2028`
-- Item 1 is the default item of its Part (group 2, fork FS2 taken): it applies to an applicant no other open item fits.  So with the experience item open (16.7.2028) item 1 is not offered, and
-- once the note has lapsed (17.7.2028) the experienced applicant falls back to item 1.  (The alternative FS2a, item 1 only for applicants with no prior training or experience at all, would leave this applicant in no item on 17.7.2028.)
#ASSERT NOT any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number` EQUALS 1) `the items open on 16 July 2028`
#ASSERT any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number` EQUALS 1) `the items open on 17 July 2028`

§§ `S13. The fees, by vintage and by head of s.59 (groups 8, 7)`

-- The Fees Regulations as made, on 1.12.2025 (before the first update day, 1.1.2026): the figures of the gazette.
#ASSERT `int — the fee in the vintage for the service on the day` `the Fees Regulations as made` `the service of sitting a practical exam` (YMD 2025 12 1) EMPTY EQUALS JUST 194
#ASSERT `int — the fee in the vintage for the service on the day` `the Fees Regulations as made` `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` (YMD 2025 12 1) EMPTY EQUALS JUST 284
#ASSERT `int — the fee in the vintage for the service on the day` `the Fees Regulations as made` `the service of filing an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal` (YMD 2025 12 1) EMPTY EQUALS JUST 398
#ASSERT `int — the fee in the vintage for the service on the day` `the Fees Regulations as made` `the service of objecting to the score of a practical exam` (YMD 2025 12 1) EMPTY EQUALS JUST 40
-- Silence: a vintage silent on a service answers silence, never a figure from another vintage.
#ASSERT `int — the fee in the vintage for the service on the day` `the Fees Regulations as made` `the service of filing an application for a licence or its renewal` (YMD 2025 12 1) EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `int — the fee in the vintage for the service on the day` `the Fees Regulations as made` `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` (YMD 2025 12 1) EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `int — the fee in the vintage for the service on the day` `the Fees Regulations as made` `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` (YMD 2025 12 1) EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `int — the fee in the vintage for the service on the day` `the Fees Regulations as made` `the service of objecting to the score of a theoretical exam` (YMD 2025 12 1) EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `int — the fee in the vintage for the service on the day` `the Fees Regulations as made` `the service of attending a continuing training course` (YMD 2025 12 1) EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
-- As amended, on 5.5.2026, with the readings of list F: regulation 3(a) updated the old amounts on 1.1.2026 by 101.25/100; the new theoretical fee took effect on 4.5.2026 and has its first update day on 1.1.2027.
#ASSERT `int — the fee in the vintage for the service on the day` `the Fees Regulations as amended` `the service of sitting a practical exam` (YMD 2026 5 5) `fixture: the index readings for the fees` EQUALS JUST 196
#ASSERT `int — the fee in the vintage for the service on the day` `the Fees Regulations as amended` `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` (YMD 2026 5 5) `fixture: the index readings for the fees` EQUALS JUST 288
#ASSERT `int — the fee in the vintage for the service on the day` `the Fees Regulations as amended` `the service of filing an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal` (YMD 2026 5 5) `fixture: the index readings for the fees` EQUALS JUST 403
#ASSERT `int — the fee in the vintage for the service on the day` `the Fees Regulations as amended` `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` (YMD 2026 5 5) `fixture: the index readings for the fees` EQUALS JUST 158
#ASSERT `int — the fee in the vintage for the service on the day` `the Fees Regulations as amended` `the service of objecting to the score of a practical exam` (YMD 2026 5 5) `fixture: the index readings for the fees` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The as-made text on 5.5.2026 needs the readings; without them the update cannot be computed.
#ASSERT REFUSED `int — the fee in the vintage for the service on the day` `the Fees Regulations as made` `the service of sitting a practical exam` (YMD 2026 5 5) EMPTY
-- Which text was in force.
#ASSERT `int — the vintage of the Fees Regulations in force on the day` (YMD 2025 7 15) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `int — the vintage of the Fees Regulations in force on the day` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS JUST `the Fees Regulations as made`
#ASSERT `int — the vintage of the Fees Regulations in force on the day` (YMD 2026 5 3) EQUALS JUST `the Fees Regulations as made`
#ASSERT `int — the vintage of the Fees Regulations in force on the day` (YMD 2026 5 4) EQUALS JUST `the Fees Regulations as amended`
-- The nine services fall under the six heads of s.59: one head holds the four exam services, each of the others one.
#ASSERT count `int — every service under the Fees Regulations` EQUALS 9
#ASSERT count (`s 59 — the heads of fee for which the Minister may set a fee`) EQUALS 6
#ASSERT count (`int — the services that fall under the head` `a fee for the examinations required for a final certificate, including an objection to an examination`) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT count (`int — the services that fall under the head` `a fee for submitting an application for a licence`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT count (`int — the services that fall under the head` `a fee for the grant of a licence, or for its renewal`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT count (`int — the services that fall under the head` `a fee for the continuing training under section 17`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT count (`int — the services that fall under the head` `a different rate of fee for submitting an application for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or for its renewal`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT count (`int — the services that fall under the head` `a different rate of fee for the grant of a temporary licence for a foreign expert`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT all (GIVEN head YIELD elem head (`s 59 — the heads of fee for which the Minister may set a fee`)) (map (GIVEN service YIELD `int — the head of fee under section 59 for the service` service) `int — every service under the Fees Regulations`)
-- Each head has at least one service group 8 can price.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN head YIELD NOT null (`int — the services that fall under the head` head)) (`s 59 — the heads of fee for which the Minister may set a fee`)
-- The heads each vintage prices.
#ASSERT count (`int — the heads of fee the vintage prices` `the Fees Regulations as made`) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT count (`int — the heads of fee the vintage prices` `the Fees Regulations as amended`) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT count (`int — the heads of fee the vintage prices` `the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations`) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `int — the vintage prices the head` `the Fees Regulations as made` `a fee for the grant of a licence, or for its renewal`
#ASSERT NOT `int — the vintage prices the head` `the Fees Regulations as made` `a fee for submitting an application for a licence`
#ASSERT NOT `int — the vintage prices the head` `the Fees Regulations as amended` `a different rate of fee for the grant of a temporary licence for a foreign expert`
#ASSERT `int — the vintage prices the head` `the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations` `a fee for submitting an application for a licence`
#ASSERT NOT `int — the vintage prices the head` `the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations` `a fee for the grant of a licence, or for its renewal`
-- No vintage prices the continuing training of s.17 (a power not exercised is silence, not conflict).
#ASSERT NOT `int — the vintage prices the head` `the Fees Regulations as made` `a fee for the continuing training under section 17`
#ASSERT NOT `int — the vintage prices the head` `the Fees Regulations as amended` `a fee for the continuing training under section 17`
#ASSERT NOT `int — the vintage prices the head` `the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations` `a fee for the continuing training under section 17`

§§ `S23. The owner's ruling on day X, the default: the later of the two dates, 16 July 2025 (groups 7, 8, 2)`

-- Written from the Hebrew text and the ruling of 2026-10-14 before it was run.  Publication 14.1.2025; the section 59 regulations in force 16.7.2025 (regulation 5: seven days from 9.7.2025).
-- Default reading of s.63(a)(1): the later of two DATES, three months from publication (14.4.2025) and 16.7.2025, so day X is 16.7.2025.
-- Paragraph (2): 18 months from day X, 16.1.2027, a Saturday; IL s.10(c) is not applied to a commencement counted from another date (group 7, fork F-C-1).
-- The Second Schedule's three-year notes: three years from day X end on 16.7.2028; an application on 17.7.2028 is outside them, and so is one on 16.10.2028.
`the items open on 16 October 2028` MEANS `int — the training the Second Schedule requires for` (`fixture: an application by` `the applicant with the year 2027 of work` `for a` `grade 1 licence` `on` (YMD 2028 10 16))
#ASSERT `int — the commencement day` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
#ASSERT `int — the day the Law commences for work on a system with any other refrigerant` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 16
-- The schedule route: the experience item (item 2) is open on 16.7.2028 and closed after it, so item 1 takes over; on the later day the alternative would keep it open, it is closed.
#ASSERT any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number` EQUALS 2) `the items open on 16 July 2028`
#ASSERT NOT any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number` EQUALS 2) `the items open on 17 July 2028`
#ASSERT NOT any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number` EQUALS 2) `the items open on 16 October 2028`
#ASSERT any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number` EQUALS 1) `the items open on 16 October 2028`
-- The regime of paragraph (2): an R134a system is reached on 16.1.2027 and not on 15.1.2027; lawful propane (paragraph (1)) from 16.7.2025 and not before.
#ASSERT NOT `int — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a") (YMD 2027 1 15)
#ASSERT `int — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a") (YMD 2027 1 16)
#ASSERT `int — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a") (YMD 2027 4 16)
#ASSERT NOT `int — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "290") (YMD 2025 7 15)
#ASSERT `int — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "290") (YMD 2025 7 16)

§§ `S24. The owner's ruling on day X, the documented alternative: three months from the later of the two days, 16 October 2025 (groups 7, 8, 2)`

-- Written from the Hebrew text and the ruling of 2026-10-14 before it was run.  The alternative reading of s.63(a)(1): "three months from" governs both limbs, so the three months run from the LATER of the two days (publication 14.1.2025;
-- the section 59 regulations in force 16.7.2025), and day X is 16.7.2025 plus three months, 16.10.2025.  Callable, not the default.
-- Paragraph (2): 18 months from 16.10.2025 is 16.4.2027.  The Second Schedule's three-year notes: three years from 16.10.2025 end on 16.10.2028.
-- The Fees Regulations do not move: regulation 5 is a date of its own, 16.7.2025.
`the alternative: the items open on 17 October 2028` MEANS `int (three months from the later of the two days) — the training the Second Schedule requires for` (`fixture: an application by` `the applicant with the year 2027 of work` `for a` `grade 1 licence` `on` (YMD 2028 10 17))
`the alternative: the items open on 16 July 2028` MEANS `int (three months from the later of the two days) — the training the Second Schedule requires for` (`fixture: an application by` `the applicant with the year 2027 of work` `for a` `grade 1 licence` `on` (YMD 2028 7 16))
`the alternative: the items open on 17 July 2028` MEANS `int (three months from the later of the two days) — the training the Second Schedule requires for` (`fixture: an application by` `the applicant with the year 2027 of work` `for a` `grade 1 licence` `on` (YMD 2028 7 17))
`the alternative: the items open on 16 October 2028` MEANS `int (three months from the later of the two days) — the training the Second Schedule requires for` (`fixture: an application by` `the applicant with the year 2027 of work` `for a` `grade 1 licence` `on` (YMD 2028 10 16))
#ASSERT `int (three months from the later of the two days) — the commencement day` EQUALS YMD 2025 10 16
#ASSERT `int (three months from the later of the two days) — the day the Law commences for work on a system with any other refrigerant` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 16
-- The schedule route: the experience item is still open on 17.7.2028, which the default has closed, and on 16.10.2028; it is closed on 17.10.2028 and item 1 takes over.
#ASSERT any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number` EQUALS 2) `the alternative: the items open on 16 July 2028`
#ASSERT any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number` EQUALS 2) `the alternative: the items open on 17 July 2028`
#ASSERT any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number` EQUALS 2) `the alternative: the items open on 16 October 2028`
#ASSERT NOT any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number` EQUALS 1) `the alternative: the items open on 16 October 2028`
#ASSERT NOT any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number` EQUALS 2) `the alternative: the items open on 17 October 2028`
#ASSERT any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number` EQUALS 1) `the alternative: the items open on 17 October 2028`
-- The regime of paragraph (2): an R134a system is reached on 16.4.2027, not on 16.1.2027 (the default's day) and not on 15.4.2027.
#ASSERT NOT `int (three months from the later of the two days) — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a") (YMD 2027 1 16)
#ASSERT NOT `int (three months from the later of the two days) — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a") (YMD 2027 4 15)
#ASSERT `int (three months from the later of the two days) — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a") (YMD 2027 4 16)
-- Lawful propane (paragraph (1)) is reached on 16.10.2025, not on 16.7.2025 (the default's day) and not on 15.10.2025.
#ASSERT NOT `int (three months from the later of the two days) — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "290") (YMD 2025 7 16)
#ASSERT NOT `int (three months from the later of the two days) — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "290") (YMD 2025 10 15)
#ASSERT `int (three months from the later of the two days) — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "290") (YMD 2025 10 16)
-- The Fees Regulations are unaffected by the choice: they came into force on 16.7.2025 on either reading.
#ASSERT `int — the Fees Regulations came into force on` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16

§§ `S25. The two readings of day X side by side: the same applicant and the same days (groups 7, 2)`

-- Written from the Hebrew text and the ruling of 2026-10-14 before it was run.  The applicant is the one with a year of work in 2027, seeking a grade 1 licence; the system is a 10 kW R134a system.
-- The experience item (item 2) is open while the application day is within three years of day X: to 16.7.2028 by the default (day X 16.7.2025), to 16.10.2028 by the alternative (day X 16.10.2025).
--   application on 17.7.2028:  default closed, alternative open.   on 16.10.2028: default closed, alternative open.   on 17.10.2028: closed on both.
-- Paragraph (2) binds R134a work from 18 months after day X: 16.1.2027 by the default, 16.4.2027 by the alternative.
--   work on 16.1.2027: default yes, alternative no.   on 15.4.2027: default yes, alternative no.   on 16.4.2027: yes on both.
`the experience item is open on the day by the default` MEANS GIVEN day YIELD any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number` EQUALS 2) (`int — the training the Second Schedule requires for` (`fixture: an application by` `the applicant with the year 2027 of work` `for a` `grade 1 licence` `on` day))
`the experience item is open on the day by the alternative` MEANS GIVEN day YIELD any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number` EQUALS 2) (`int (three months from the later of the two days) — the training the Second Schedule requires for` (`fixture: an application by` `the applicant with the year 2027 of work` `for a` `grade 1 licence` `on` day))
`the R134a system` MEANS `fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a"
#ASSERT NOT `the experience item is open on the day by the default` (YMD 2028 7 17)
#ASSERT `the experience item is open on the day by the alternative` (YMD 2028 7 17)
#ASSERT NOT `the experience item is open on the day by the default` (YMD 2028 10 16)
#ASSERT `the experience item is open on the day by the alternative` (YMD 2028 10 16)
#ASSERT NOT `the experience item is open on the day by the default` (YMD 2028 10 17)
#ASSERT NOT `the experience item is open on the day by the alternative` (YMD 2028 10 17)
#ASSERT `int — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` `the R134a system` (YMD 2027 1 16)
#ASSERT NOT `int (three months from the later of the two days) — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` `the R134a system` (YMD 2027 1 16)
#ASSERT `int — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` `the R134a system` (YMD 2027 4 15)
#ASSERT NOT `int (three months from the later of the two days) — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` `the R134a system` (YMD 2027 4 15)
#ASSERT `int — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` `the R134a system` (YMD 2027 4 16)
#ASSERT `int (three months from the later of the two days) — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` `the R134a system` (YMD 2027 4 16)
